  "verbalization": "The visible evidence from the dataset suggests that Promazine may be associated with Allergic Rhinitis through a series of indirect pathways. Promazine is indicated for Common Cold, which is linked to Potassium Iodide and Chlorcyclizine, both of which are also linked to Allergic Rhinitis. Similarly, Promazine is indicated for Atopic Conjunctivitis, which is associated with Quifenadine, another entity linked to Allergic Rhinitis. These pathways indicate that Promazine may exert some influence on the development or manifestation of Allergic Rhinitis through its interactions with other entities in the network. The scores, while similar across the paths, suggest a moderate level of confidence in the relationship, though the exact mechanism remains unclear. The evidence is consistent across multiple paths, reinforcing the potential for Promazine to be a candidate for repositioning in the treatment of Allergic Rhinitis.",
